1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,600
Your context. Your work. Your next attempt.
Connected through evidence.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:14,800
Personal life and Shippin work.
One clear view, with separate boundaries.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,700
This public walkthrough uses fictional Personal examples
and already-public work sources.

4
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:31,400
Open a source. Understand why it belongs here.
Keep the original revision within reach.

5
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:41,800
Try another home and inspect the result.
This public action is a preview for this visit.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,800
The distinction matters:
a preview and a saved decision are different.

7
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:57,400
This access-control source belongs to Shippin work.
A person confirms the correct suggestion.

8
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:06,300
Saved in HydraDB. Raindrop accepted the review event.
The original source stays in its database.

9
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:15,100
Refresh, then reopen.
The human confirmation is still there.

10
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:24,800
This decision applies to this source.
It does not silently create a rule for everything.

11
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:31,900
Six engineering disciplines. Seven recorded relationships.
Open the knowledge behind a specialist.

12
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:37,500
TypeScript opens its research origin
and source-backed avenues.

13
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:45,700
Inspect the questions before relying on them.
Draft research remains explicitly marked as draft.

14
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:52,800
A relationship is inspectable evidence,
with a direction and an origin.

15
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:59,100
Existing Work context comes from Qdrant Cloud.
The destination is the Shippin HydraDB database.

16
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:09,500
Inspect the source and its public revision.
Its identity stays attached to the imported knowledge.

17
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,800
These three Work records are indexed in HydraDB.
The interface shows each record’s last import.

18
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:24,200
Now use the same discipline to build RRFLOW.
Main-branch changes trigger configured source sync.

19
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:32,000
The checkpoint links the public workflow and commit.
HydraDB owns the recorded synchronization state.

20
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:40,500
This read shows 111 searchable sources,
with 103 finished through every indexing stage.

21
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:48,600
This incremental run found zero changed files.
It did not freshly ingest all 111 sources.

22
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:56,800
Source changes, checks and native request IDs
remain available for inspection.

23
00:02:57,300 --> 00:03:02,800
The latest CI observation was captured automatically.
Forty-one actual checks, tied to commit 06c7de09.

24
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:10,700
Open the versioned evidence schema.
It records outcomes; it does not invent a diagnosis.

25
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:20,800
Inspect the passing graph regression check
and its pinned source assertion.

26
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:29,500
An earlier, imported CI case became a reviewed lesson:
a broad alert selector matched two messages.

27
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:37,600
The reviewed correction targets the intended alert.
A linked later run passed that same check.

28
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:44,800
The failure, correction and follow-up stay together.
A person reviewed this lesson; code was not fixed autonomously.

29
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:53,300
Ask for the reviewed failure-state UI practice.
Search only the saved lesson collection.

30
00:03:53,600 --> 00:04:01,800
HydraDB returns the reviewed lesson as one result.
The diagnosis and correction travel with it.

31
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:10,200
The practice is specific: scope the alert check
to its intended region and error message.

32
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:19,800
The next developer can inspect and reuse this context.
Retrieval is demonstrated; an automatic code change is not.

33
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:26,000
Raindrop accepted the workflow event: HTTP 200.
The recorded event identity is visible.

34
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:34,500
Native request IDs connect this status
to the same synchronization evidence.

35
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:42,800
Delivery, saved evidence and reviewed practice are distinct.
An accepted event alone does not prove improved quality.
